# Supabase — create a free project at https://supabase.com and paste in values below
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Admin access — comma-separated emails allowed into /admin (the manual RMB
# review queue). Must match an email that has a real account in this app.
ADMIN_EMAILS=

# Resend (resend.com) — sends the new-KYC-submission alert to every ADMIN_EMAILS address (see
# src/lib/actions/kyc.ts). Sender is notifications@jesdanpay.net; verifying that domain in
# Resend's dashboard is a manual step outside this codebase. A missing/invalid key just makes the
# send fail silently (logged, never blocks a KYC submission) rather than breaking anything.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Klasha — GHS deposit collection only (initiateKlashaDeposit). NGN moved to Busha once it was
# confirmed working live there, while Klasha's own account access stayed blocked (403) the
# entire time this was built. Klasha's CNY payout API was also investigated but confirmed by
# their own team to be merchant-only (pay Klasha's own vendors from their dashboard, not
# resellable to end customers via API) — removed. See src/lib/klasha/client.ts.
#
# Auth is a real account login (POST /auth/account/v2/login with these two), NOT an API key
# sent as a bearer token — confirmed on a support call and against
# developers.klasha.com/overview/authentication. The returned JWT is cached and sent alongside
# KLASHA_PUBLIC_KEY as x-auth-token on every request (the login call itself now also sends
# x-auth-token — confirmed required by Klasha support); see client.ts's header comment.
KLASHA_LOGIN_EMAIL=
KLASHA_LOGIN_PASSWORD=
# This is currently Klasha's SANDBOX host, confirmed by Klasha support (Jeremiah) — NOT
# production. Must be changed to Klasha's live base URL when going to production; until then,
# KLASHA_LOGIN_EMAIL/KLASHA_LOGIN_PASSWORD/KLASHA_PUBLIC_KEY/KLASHA_ENCRYPTION_SECRET below must
# all be the SANDBOX account's values — production credentials do not work against this host.
# Swap all five together (base URL + all four credentials) when going live.
KLASHA_API_BASE_URL=https://dev.kcookery.com
KLASHA_PUBLIC_KEY=

# Klasha request-body encryption secret — 3DES-CBC, must be exactly 24 bytes (see
# src/lib/klasha/client.ts's encryptBody()). From Klasha Dashboard > Settings.
KLASHA_ENCRYPTION_SECRET=

# The value entered into the Klasha dashboard's webhook config "Enter your webhook key" field.
# Checked (non-blockingly — a mismatch is logged, never rejected) against a short list of
# plausible header names in src/app/api/webhooks/klasha/route.ts, since the real header/scheme
# is still unconfirmed by any real delivery or by Klasha's docs/support. Every incoming header +
# raw body is also still logged to webhook_events so the real scheme can be reverse-engineered
# once a real signed delivery lands, same discipline as BUSHA_WEBHOOK_SECRET below.
KLASHA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Public URL of this app, used as the redirect target after a Klasha GHS deposit (Klasha's
# hosted payment page sends the customer back here when they're done). Must be a real HTTPS
# URL once deployed — localhost only works for local testing where Klasha can still reach it.
# No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — this is only ever read server-side (src/lib/actions/klasha.ts),
# so it doesn't need to (and shouldn't) ship into the client bundle.
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Google Analytics (GA4) measurement ID — src/components/analytics/GoogleAnalytics.tsx. Only set
# in Production on Vercel; left blank everywhere else (local dev, preview deploys) since the
# component renders nothing at all when this is unset. Even when set, it only actually tracks on
# public marketing/auth pages (see that file) — admin and dashboard routes carry user IDs and
# financial data and must never reach a third party.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# Busha — deposit + swap API for NGN, KES, and USDT (docs.busha.io) — confirmed live on all
# three; GHS is rejected outright by this account ("Invalid Currency GHS") so GHS deposits go
# through Klasha instead (see above). Use the SECRET key from your Busha dashboard, not the
# public one (the public key is client-side only and will be rejected by these server-side
# calls). Confirmed live only against the production host below — the documented sandbox host
# (api.sandbox.busha.so) rejected a real Busha Business account's secret key entirely, so a
# real registered business account may only work against production.
BUSHA_API_KEY=
BUSHA_API_BASE_URL=https://api.busha.io

# Busha webhook shared secret. An earlier version of this check used a guessed header name and
# silently rejected every real webhook (see src/app/api/webhooks/busha/route.ts's header comment
# for the full story) — that mistake is why this is checked non-blockingly now: real deliveries
# have since confirmed the actual header (`x-bu-signature`, HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body against
# this secret, base64-encoded), but a mismatch is still only logged, never rejected, until that's
# independently confirmed against Busha's own docs/support rather than this codebase's own
# reverse-engineering of captured traffic. The real completion/failure of a transaction no longer
# depends on this at all either way — see that route's SECURITY comment for the getTransfer-based
# fix that actually closed the forgery gap.
BUSHA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Shared secret for the deposit-reconciliation endpoint (src/app/api/cron/reconcile-deposits).
# NOT called by Vercel's own Cron — the Hobby plan only allows a once-per-day schedule and
# rejects the deployment outright if vercel.json asks for anything more frequent (confirmed:
# this silently broke every deployment from the commit that first added vercel.json onward).
# Instead, use a free external scheduler (e.g. cron-job.org) to hit this URL every 15 minutes
# with header `Authorization: Bearer <this value>`. Set this same value in Vercel's project env
# vars (Settings > Environment Variables). Leaving it unset allows any caller through — fine for
# local testing, not for production.
CRON_SECRET=
